# At unit level every `name:` begins a definition, so a call written with its
# labelled arguments on the definition's line is cut in pieces: `T: S.substring
# from: 2 to: 3` is three definitions, and the first reads the method with no
# arguments. When each missing argument is written after it on its line, the
# hint shows the call in parentheses; when one is not, the usual hint stands.
S: "abcdef"
L: list {1 2 3}
T: S.substring from: 2 to: 3
E: L.get i: 1
U: S.startsWith other: "a"
main: function is {
    print "unreached"
}
